Root cause:
The bug was caused by the incorrect referencing of the device structure in the sysfs entry functions. The code was using the current device (`dev`) instead of the parent device (`dev->parent`), leading to crashes when accessing device-specific data that did not belong to the current device context.

Code statements information:
The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
struct ds1685_priv *rtc = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
```
Reason:
This line retrieves the driver data associated with the current device (`dev`), which is incorrect because the sysfs entry functions should reference the parent device instead. This leads to accessing device-specific data that does not belong to the current device context, causing crashes.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
struct ds1685_priv *rtc = dev_get_drvdata(dev->parent);
```
Reason:
This line correctly retrieves the driver data associated with the parent device (`dev->parent`), ensuring that the sysfs entry functions access the appropriate device context. This change prevents crashes by ensuring that the correct device-specific data is accessed.


